---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import LumensKelvinIrcTool from '../../components/LumensKelvinIrcTool.astro';
---
<Layout title="Lighting simulator: lumens, colour temperature and CRI room by room | 1 pièce 1 ampoule" description="See how lumens, colour temperature (Kelvin) and CRI change the look of a living room, bedroom, kitchen, bathroom, home office or garage, before you buy a bulb.">
  <section class="mt-10">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-amber-700">Free tool</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl text-stone-900 sm:text-4xl">Lighting simulator, room by room</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-stone-600">See it before you buy: how many lumens, which shade of white and what CRI your room needs. For the details behind it: <a class="font-semibold text-amber-700" href="/en/guides/lumens-vs-watts/">lumens vs watts</a>, <a class="font-semibold text-amber-700" href="/en/guides/colour-temperature-kelvin/">colour temperature</a>, <a class="font-semibold text-amber-700" href="/en/guides/cri-colour-rendering-index/">CRI</a>, <a class="font-semibold text-amber-700" href="/en/tutorials/how-much-light-per-room-lux-foot-candles/">how much light per room</a>.</p>
  </section>
  <LumensKelvinIrcTool lang="en" />
  <section class="mt-10 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm"><h2 class="text-lg text-stone-900">Garage and workshop</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-stone-600">Plenty of light, neutral or cool white, and a high CRI if you need to see detail: tools, markings, paint.</p></div>
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm"><h2 class="text-lg text-stone-900">Living room and bedroom</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-stone-600">Warm white at medium output, with a dimmer for the evening. Several light sources beat one bright ceiling light.</p></div>
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm"><h2 class="text-lg text-stone-900">Where the figures come from</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-stone-600">The ranges are based on usual illuminance levels (lux) multiplied by a typical floor area. Treat the result as a guide: a screen cannot reproduce real light exactly.</p></div>
  </section>
</Layout>
